## 9. Honest framing for the write-up

What the results actually support:

- The symbolic constraint layer produces a large, statistically strong
  improvement in Causal Consistency (0.281 → 0.641, p≈2e-7, 24 improvements and
  0 regressions), reproduced on held-out rule families.
- The base model has high accuracy on unsafe cases (0.891) and poor accuracy on
  safe ones (0.297) — it is over-cautious rather than clinically discriminating.
  Plain accuracy hides this; pair-level Causal Consistency exposes it. This is
  the strongest argument for the proposal's metric choice.
- RAG showed no significant benefit on this benchmark (pending the retrieval
  diagnostic in P3).
- Entropy-based uncertainty quantification failed, with an inverted signal. This
  falsifies an assumption in §4.7.

What must be disclosed:

- Thresholds are hand-written and not yet sourced from FDA/UMLS.
- The symbolic gate is post-hoc, not the proposal's residual-stream layer.
- The benchmark was hardened after an initial saturated result.
- Held-out has only 16 pairs; its confidence intervals are very wide.
- Aims 1 and 2 have not been started.

Reporting the negative results is not a weakness. A proposal that lists
falsifiable predictions and then reports one as falsified is doing what it said
it would do.